          "instructions": "Part 2: Questions 11 \u2013 16Choose the correct letter, A, B or C.",
          "shared_content_html": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">11. Heather says pottery differs from other art forms because</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>A</strong> it lasts longer in the ground.</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>B</strong> it is practised by more people.</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>C</strong> it can be repaired more easily.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">12. Archaeologists sometimes identify the use of ancient pottery from</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>A</strong> the clay it was made with.</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>B</strong> the marks that are on it.</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>C</strong> the basic shape of it.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">13. Some people join Heather\u2019s pottery class because they want to</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>A</strong> create an item that looks very old.</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>B</strong> find something that they are good at.</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>C</strong> make something that will outlive them.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">14. What does Heather value most about being a potter?</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>A</strong> its calming effect</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>B</strong> its messy nature</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>C</strong> its physical benefits</span></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">15. Most of the visitors to Edelman Pottery</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>A</strong> bring friends to join courses.</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>B</strong> have never made a pot before.</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>C</strong> try to learn techniques too quickly.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">16. Heather reminds her visitors that they should</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>A</strong> put on their aprons.</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>B</strong> change their clothes.</span><br/>\n<span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><input type=\"checkbox\"/>C</strong> take off their jewellery.</span></p>",
