      "title": "Reading Passage 3",
      "content_html": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In the past it was essential to hoard our calories for as long as possible because our food source was mainly restricted to 29 __________ and 30__________ which brought in irregular supplies. However, these reserves were intended for 31__________ because they had the power and energy to work hard. Nowadays, the focus has moved away from jobs on 32__________ and in 33__________ to jobs that weren\u2019t available 34__________ . Through technology, it has now become possible to replace many body 35__________ and as techniques improve we will be able to develop better 36__________ .</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In the future, a nanobot\u2019s ability to redesign our digestive system will be 37__________ . One function is the intelligent 38__________ of the exact nutritional requirements needed. If this all seems to be fantasy, consider a tiny machine already developed that has now been used in the treatment of 39__________ However, this has not been tried on 40__________</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A</strong> Parkinson\u2019s<br/><strong>B</strong> haemophilia<br/><strong>C</strong> diabetes<br/><strong>D</strong> humans<br/><strong>E</strong> radical<br/><strong>F</strong> rats<br/><strong>G</strong> extract<br/><strong>H</strong> radically<br/><strong>I</strong> extraction<br/><strong>J</strong> cells</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><input bg_collapse_expand=\"6abcf2de559336013662704\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"6abcf2de559336013662704\"/><input id=\"bg-show-more-text-6abcf2de559336013662704\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"Show Answers\"/><input id=\"bg-show-less-text-6abcf2de559336013662704\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"Hide Answers\"/></p><p style=\"text-align: justify\">1. False<br/>2. True<br/>3. Not Given<br/>4. False<br/>5. B<br/>6. B<br/>7. A<br/>8. G<br/>9. vii<br/>10. iii<br/>11. vi<br/>12. ix<br/>13. ii<br/>14. G<br/>15. C<br/>16. H<br/>17. B<br/>18. C<br/>19. E<br/>20. True<br/>21. True<br/>22. False<br/>23. Not Given<br/>24. acoustic quality<br/>25. research centre<br/>26. experimental psychology<br/>27. (relevant) task<br/>28. statistical analysis<br/>29. foraging<br/>30. hunting<br/>31. labourers<br/>32. farms<br/>33. factories<br/>34. century ago<br/>35. parts<br/>36. systems<br/>37. E<br/>38. I<br/>39. C<br/>40. D</p><p style=\"text-align: justify\"></p>",
