      "passage_number": 3,
      "title": "Reading Passage 3",
      "content_html": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>List of headings</strong><br/>i Not as big, but needing just enough<br/>ii Some attitudes to blood<br/>iii Good, but not so quick<br/>iv Two ideas see a wrong conclusion<br/>v Complicated identification<br/>vi An interesting treatment<br/>vii A shorter life, but just as important<br/>viii The Principal part that adds some colour<br/>ix Bone marrow and blood<br/>x Maintaining supplies</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Example Paragraph A Answer ii</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">27. Paragraph B<br/>28. Paragraph C<br/>29. Paragraph D<br/>30. Paragraph E<br/>31. Paragraph F<br/>32. Paragraph G<br/>33. Paragraph H</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><figure style=\"text-align: justify;\"><table><thead><tr><th>Blood component</th><th>Associated fact</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Red cells</td><td>upon dying, dealt with by (34)\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026</td></tr><tr><td>White cells</td><td>require (35)\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026.before attacking invaders</td></tr><tr><td>Platelets</td><td>their numbers need careful (36)\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026.</td></tr><tr><td>(37)\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026..</td><td>many varieties exist</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>TRUE</strong> if the statement agrees with the information<br/><strong>FALSE</strong> if the statement contradicts the information<br/><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> If there is no information on this</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">38. Blood cross-matching can be done without special equipment.<br/>39. In poorer countries, family members often donate blood.<br/>40. Bleeding people was a painful process.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br/><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"7372142965\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><input bg_collapse_expand=\"6abd11670478b3033657474\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"6abd11670478b3033657474\"/><input id=\"bg-show-more-text-6abd11670478b3033657474\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"Show Answers\"/><input id=\"bg-show-less-text-6abd11670478b3033657474\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"Hide Answers\"/></p><p style=\"text-align: justify\">1. disgusting appearance<br/>2. domestic hygiene<br/>3. wasp<br/>4. flatten (bodies)<br/>5. false<br/>6. true<br/>7. false<br/>8. NG<br/>9. Pheromones<br/>10. co-operate<br/>11. admiration<br/>12. D<br/>13. B<br/>14. True<br/>15. NG<br/>16. True<br/>17. (the) bishop<br/>18. (to) accelerate play<br/>19. (Garry) Kasparov<br/>20. subliminal memory<br/>21. theoretical study<br/>22. huge population<br/>23. faster processing<br/>24. intelligence<br/>25. B<br/>26. C<br/>27. viii<br/>28. vii<br/>29. i<br/>30. v<br/>31. iii<br/>32. x<br/>33. iv<br/>34. spleen and liver<br/>35. sufficient numbers<br/>36. regulation<br/>37. antigens<br/>38. false<br/>39. true<br/>40. NG</p><p style=\"text-align: justify\"></p>",
