      "title": "Reading Passage 3",
      "content_html": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A diagram that explains the mechanism and working principles of roller coaster.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"aligncenter\" data-lazyloaded=\"1\" data-src=\"../wp-content/uploads/2024/09/186-test-aca-1.png\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"378\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODdhAQABAPAAAMPDwwAAACwAAAAAAQABAAACAkQBADs=\" width=\"606\"/><noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"aligncenter\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"378\" src=\"../wp-content/uploads/2024/09/186-test-aca-1.png\" width=\"606\"/></noscript></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The first roller coaster was perhaps originated from Russia which is wrapped up by (31)\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026.which was introduced into France, and it was modified to (32)\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026.because temperature there would (33)\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026the ice. This time (34)\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026..were installed on the board. In America, the first roller coaster was said to appear in Pennsylvania, it was actually a railroad which was designed to send (35)\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026between two mountains. Josiah White turned it into a thrill ride, it was also called switch back track and a (36)\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026\u2026..there allowed riders to slide downward back again.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>YES</strong> if the statement agrees with the views of the writer<br/>\n<strong>NO</strong> if the statement contradicts the views of the writer<br/>\n<strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">37. The most exiting roller coaster in the world is in New Jersey.<br/>\n38. French added more innovation on Russian ice slide including both cars and tracks.<br/>\n39. Switch Back Railways began to gain popularity since its first construction in New York.<br/>\n40. The Great Depression affected amusement parks yet did not shake the significant role of US roller coasters in the world.</p><p><br/>\n<ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5477565220\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins><br/>\n<input bg_collapse_expand=\"6abcb817ade031004761204\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"6abcb817ade031004761204\"/><input id=\"bg-show-more-text-6abcb817ade031004761204\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"Show Answers\"/><input id=\"bg-show-less-text-6abcb817ade031004761204\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"Hide Answers\"/></p><p>1. D<br/>\n2. C<br/>\n3. C<br/>\n4. B<br/>\n5. microwave dish<br/>\n6. accelerometers<br/>\n7. steel girders<br/>\n8. flange<br/>\n9. C<br/>\n10. H<br/>\n11. G<br/>\n12. B<br/>\n13. E<br/>\n14. A<br/>\n15. B<br/>\n16. C<br/>\n17. D<br/>\n18. NG<br/>\n19. True<br/>\n20. NG<br/>\n21. False<br/>\n22. C<br/>\n23. B<br/>\n24. C<br/>\n25. A<br/>\n26. B<br/>\n27. Chain<br/>\n28. Loop<br/>\n29. Gears<br/>\n30. (simple) motor<br/>\n31. Ice<br/>\n32. Waxed slices<br/>\n33. Melt<br/>\n34. Wheels<br/>\n35. Coal<br/>\n36. Steam engine<br/>\n37. NG<br/>\n38. Yes<br/>\n39. Yes<br/>\n40. No<br/></p>",
