      "content_html": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">28. What is the major way for local people make barely support of living in Muthukandiya village?<br/>\n29. Where can adult workers make extra money from in daytime?<br/>\n30. What has been dug to supply water for daily household life?<br/>\n31. In which year did the plan of a new project to lessen the effect of drought begins?<br/>\n32. Where do the gutters and pipes collect rainwater from?<br/>\n33. What helps the family obtain more water for domestic needs than those relying on only wells and ponds?</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>YES</strong>\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 if the statement agrees with the views of the writer<br/>\n<strong>NO</strong>\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0if the statement contradicts the views of the writer<br/>\n<strong>NOT GIVEN</strong>\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">34. Most of the government\u2019s actions and other programs have somewhat failed.<br/>\n35. Masons were trained for the constructing parts of the rainwater harvesting system.<br/>\n36. The cost of rainwater harvesting systems was shared by local villagers and the local government.<br/>\n37. Tanks increase both the amount and quality of the water for domestic use.<br/>\n38. To send her daughter to school, a widow had to work for a job in a rainwater harvesting scheme.<br/>\n39. Households benefited began to pay part of the maintenance or repairs.<br/>\n40. Training two masons at the same time is much more preferable to training a single one.</p><p><br/>\n<ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"7372142965\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins><br/>\n<input bg_collapse_expand=\"6abc56e57eef83045779549\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"6abc56e57eef83045779549\"/><input id=\"bg-show-more-text-6abc56e57eef83045779549\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"Show Answers\"/><input id=\"bg-show-less-text-6abc56e57eef83045779549\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"Hide Answers\"/></p><p>1. D<br/>\n2. H<br/>\n3. A<br/>\n4. G<br/>\n5. E<br/>\n6. F<br/>\n7. C<br/>\n8. B<br/>\n9. B<br/>\n10. B<br/>\n11. True<br/>\n12. False<br/>\n13. True<br/>\n14. Not given<br/>\n15. E<br/>\n16. B<br/>\n17. E<br/>\n18. F<br/>\n19. A<br/>\n20. Birch trees<br/>\n21. Russian rivers<br/>\n22. Pumps<br/>\n23. Cables<br/>\n24. Volcanic explosions<br/>\n25. C<br/>\n26. D<br/>\n27. A<br/>\n28. Crop production<br/>\n29. Sugar-cane plantations<br/>\n30. Three wells/ 3 well<br/>\n31. 1998<br/>\n32. Roofs of houses<br/>\n33. Rainwater storage tanks<br/>\n34. Not given<br/>\n35. Yes<br/>\n36. No<br/>\n37. Yes<br/>\n38. No<br/>\n39. Yes<br/>\n40. Not given</p><p></p>",
