  "test_id": "advice",
  "title": "Describe an advice you received on your subjects or work \u2013 IELTS MASTER",
  "part": "Part 2",
  "topic": "Talk about a time when you gave advice to someone",
  "content_type": "sample_answer",
  "cue_card_instructions": null,
  "prompts": [],
  "supporting_text": "<div class=\"entry-content\"><p>1. I don\u2019t consider myself experienced enough to make the important decisions of my life on my own.</p><p>2. Normally I seek the guidance of my parents because I strongly believe that parents are the best judge for us.<br/>3. They have all the experience in the world and know us inside out to make the best decision for us.<br/>4. But there was a matter on which I had to look outside my family for help.<br/>5. After completing my secondary education I was in a dilemma regarding my future choice of stream for higher education as I was presented with two major options of medical and non-medical.<br/>6. In this regard my parents could not help me much because to make this decision I needed someone who kept abreast of latest developments in the field of education as well as career opportunities available after completion of higher study.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"7372142965\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>7. Fortunately I had someone with experience and credentials to guide me on this.<br/>8. One of my uncle\u2019s daughter recently graduated from a reputed college in Canada and immediately after completing her education got a job offer from a leading IT company.<br/>9. When I approached her with my problem, she immediately asked me about my interests and my long term goal.<br/>10. I told her about my predilection for technology and accordingly she adviced me to opt for non-medical stream for my higher study.<br/>11. It was fine as far as my interest was concerned but then I inquired about career choices that I would I have if I chose non-medical.<br/>12. To be honest I was a bit sceptical about non-medical because I know few of my seniors who did engineering and were hard pressed to find suitable employment opportunities for themselves.<br/>13. I shared my apprehension with her and she acknowledged the fact that things have changed a lot in recent years.<br/>14. But she reassured me that if I choose the relevant field and performed well then there is no dearth of opportunities.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5477565220\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>15. I could not refute her argument as she was the living proof of it.<br/>16. She then apprised me of the couple of fields of technology which are growing in demand such as nanotechnology and biotechnology.<br/>17. So on her suggestion I chose non-medical and so far things are on track for me.<br/>18. I constantly keep in touch with her and seek advice on the skills that I need to acquire to give myself an edge over other students.</p></div><p>1. I don\u2019t consider myself experienced enough to make the important decisions of my life on my own.</p><p>2. Normally I seek the guidance of my parents because I strongly believe that parents are the best judge for us.<br/>3. They have all the experience in the world and know us inside out to make the best decision for us.<br/>4. But there was a matter on which I had to look outside my family for help.<br/>5. After completing my secondary education I was in a dilemma regarding my future choice of stream for higher education as I was presented with two major options of medical and non-medical.<br/>6. In this regard my parents could not help me much because to make this decision I needed someone who kept abreast of latest developments in the field of education as well as career opportunities available after completion of higher study.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"7372142965\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>7. Fortunately I had someone with experience and credentials to guide me on this.<br/>8. One of my uncle\u2019s daughter recently graduated from a reputed college in Canada and immediately after completing her education got a job offer from a leading IT company.<br/>9. When I approached her with my problem, she immediately asked me about my interests and my long term goal.<br/>10. I told her about my predilection for technology and accordingly she adviced me to opt for non-medical stream for my higher study.<br/>11. It was fine as far as my interest was concerned but then I inquired about career choices that I would I have if I chose non-medical.<br/>12. To be honest I was a bit sceptical about non-medical because I know few of my seniors who did engineering and were hard pressed to find suitable employment opportunities for themselves.<br/>13. I shared my apprehension with her and she acknowledged the fact that things have changed a lot in recent years.<br/>14. But she reassured me that if I choose the relevant field and performed well then there is no dearth of opportunities.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5477565220\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>15. I could not refute her argument as she was the living proof of it.<br/>16. She then apprised me of the couple of fields of technology which are growing in demand such as nanotechnology and biotechnology.<br/>17. So on her suggestion I chose non-medical and so far things are on track for me.<br/>18. I constantly keep in touch with her and seek advice on the skills that I need to acquire to give myself an edge over other students.</p>",
  "test_type": "UNKNOWN",
  "canonical_id": "SPE-bf6c3186-advice"
