  "supporting_text": "<div class=\"entry-content\"><p>1. Every person should have a role model to look up to.<br/>2. Since I am sports fanatic therefore I idolize sports personalities.<br/>3. There were a few prominent sports persons whom I really admired when I was growing up such as Michael Jordan in basketball, Tiger Woods in golf, Ronaldo in football.<br/>4. I was highly amazed by their athletic prowess but there was one sportsman whom I adulated for his personal traits.<br/>5. That person was Indian cricketing legend Sachin Tendulkar.<br/>6. The things I had heard about him in media and Internet were a great source of inspiration for youngsters like me.<br/>7. He was the true ambassador of attributes like sportsman spirit and fitness.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>8. He was practically the first athlete in Indian cricket who had brought focus on fitness.<br/>9. I read about his daily routine in his interview in which he mentioned that irrespective of his busy schedule he always managed to take out time for his daily workout.<br/>10. I would have loved to spend a day with him and see how he did that even after being the most sought after sports person in India.<br/>11. He also said that for him integrity and fitness were above any sporting ability because without these two qualities one cannot become a true sportsman.<br/>12. He is also known for his humility and altruistic nature.<br/>13. He is a philanthropist and runs a charity for differently abled children of our society.<br/>14. Every now and then we can see him on TV espousing a noble cause for example, abiding of traffic rules or planting more trees in our neighbourhood or girl education.<br/>15. During his peak sporting days he set an example for all other sport persons and youngsters like me when he rejected a 20 million dollar endorsement deal which was offered to him by a leading liquor brand in India.<br/>16. He rejected this deal because he felt that as a public figure he had a responsibility towards the nation and could not promote something which he knew was debilitating for our health.<br/>17. Another example of his firm belief in the importance of fitness in our lives.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>18. Last month he set another example for youngsters to follow when he announced that he had turned vegetarian and would urge other people to do the same.<br/>19. He is highly respected in our nation not only as a great sportsman but also as a great human being.</p><p>\u00a0</p><p><a href=\"../ielts-speaking-latest-makkar-cue-cards/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Latest Makkar Speaking CUE CARDS with NEW SOLUTIONS</strong></a></p></div><p>1. Every person should have a role model to look up to.<br/>2. Since I am sports fanatic therefore I idolize sports personalities.<br/>3. There were a few prominent sports persons whom I really admired when I was growing up such as Michael Jordan in basketball, Tiger Woods in golf, Ronaldo in football.<br/>4. I was highly amazed by their athletic prowess but there was one sportsman whom I adulated for his personal traits.<br/>5. That person was Indian cricketing legend Sachin Tendulkar.<br/>6. The things I had heard about him in media and Internet were a great source of inspiration for youngsters like me.<br/>7. He was the true ambassador of attributes like sportsman spirit and fitness.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>8. He was practically the first athlete in Indian cricket who had brought focus on fitness.<br/>9. I read about his daily routine in his interview in which he mentioned that irrespective of his busy schedule he always managed to take out time for his daily workout.<br/>10. I would have loved to spend a day with him and see how he did that even after being the most sought after sports person in India.<br/>11. He also said that for him integrity and fitness were above any sporting ability because without these two qualities one cannot become a true sportsman.<br/>12. He is also known for his humility and altruistic nature.<br/>13. He is a philanthropist and runs a charity for differently abled children of our society.<br/>14. Every now and then we can see him on TV espousing a noble cause for example, abiding of traffic rules or planting more trees in our neighbourhood or girl education.<br/>15. During his peak sporting days he set an example for all other sport persons and youngsters like me when he rejected a 20 million dollar endorsement deal which was offered to him by a leading liquor brand in India.<br/>16. He rejected this deal because he felt that as a public figure he had a responsibility towards the nation and could not promote something which he knew was debilitating for our health.<br/>17. Another example of his firm belief in the importance of fitness in our lives.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>18. Last month he set another example for youngsters to follow when he announced that he had turned vegetarian and would urge other people to do the same.<br/>19. He is highly respected in our nation not only as a great sportsman but also as a great human being.</p><p>\u00a0</p><p><a href=\"../ielts-speaking-latest-makkar-cue-cards/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Latest Makkar Speaking CUE CARDS with NEW SOLUTIONS</strong></a></p>",
