  "title": "Describe a practical skill you learned \u2013 IELTS MASTER",
  "part": "Part 2",
  "topic": "Talk about a time when you gave advice to someone",
  "content_type": "sample_answer",
  "cue_card_instructions": null,
  "prompts": [],
  "supporting_text": "<div class=\"entry-content\"><p>1. Education lays the foundation of a decent life for any individual.<br/>2. It should be a fundamental right for every citizen.<br/>3. I have been blessed with a family who deeply believes in the importance of education and has made sure that I have the best education possible.<br/>4. I was an above average student in my school and my favorite subjects were maths and science.<br/>5. These two subjects are paramount for intellectual growth of an individual as these challenge one\u2019s ability to think and learn.<br/>6. Maths is particularly important because of the basic practical skills it teaches us such as addition, subtraction, multiplication and division.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5477565220\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>7. These skills help us perform every day basic activities such as planning our family budget, paying for things and services that we buy and many more.<br/>8. While these basic skills are the cornerstone of any mathematical teaching, there is one particular skill which I found really interesting and useful.<br/>9. It is the ability to calculate probability.<br/>10. I was taught about the concept of probability in my elementary school.<br/>11. Probability as the name suggests is the ability to calculate the likelihood of any event.<br/>12. It is a highly complex skill to learn as it requires counterintuitive thinking to calculate probability of anything.<br/>13. But once I learnt this skill I realized how important and useful it is.<br/>14. If we think logically then every decision we make in our lives is driven by probability.<br/>15. Our decisions always have choices to make and we should make the best choice for us.<br/>16. Now how do we decide which choice is best for us.<br/>17. This decision should be made on the basis of event that is most likely to happen and which is deciphered by using the concept of probability.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"7372142965\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>18. For example recently my father decided to buy a car for the family.<br/>19. We had shortlisted two models from two different manufacturers but could not decide any further.<br/>20. That is when I used my probability skills to make the final decision.<br/>21. I gathered some data points about both the models such as service centres of each company, number of cars sold each year, number of accidents these two models were involved in.<br/>22. Then I used these data points to figure out that which car is more likely to last long with low maintenance cost using the probability method I learnt in school.</p></div><p>1. Education lays the foundation of a decent life for any individual.<br/>2. It should be a fundamental right for every citizen.<br/>3. I have been blessed with a family who deeply believes in the importance of education and has made sure that I have the best education possible.<br/>4. I was an above average student in my school and my favorite subjects were maths and science.<br/>5. These two subjects are paramount for intellectual growth of an individual as these challenge one\u2019s ability to think and learn.<br/>6. Maths is particularly important because of the basic practical skills it teaches us such as addition, subtraction, multiplication and division.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5477565220\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>7. These skills help us perform every day basic activities such as planning our family budget, paying for things and services that we buy and many more.<br/>8. While these basic skills are the cornerstone of any mathematical teaching, there is one particular skill which I found really interesting and useful.<br/>9. It is the ability to calculate probability.<br/>10. I was taught about the concept of probability in my elementary school.<br/>11. Probability as the name suggests is the ability to calculate the likelihood of any event.<br/>12. It is a highly complex skill to learn as it requires counterintuitive thinking to calculate probability of anything.<br/>13. But once I learnt this skill I realized how important and useful it is.<br/>14. If we think logically then every decision we make in our lives is driven by probability.<br/>15. Our decisions always have choices to make and we should make the best choice for us.<br/>16. Now how do we decide which choice is best for us.<br/>17. This decision should be made on the basis of event that is most likely to happen and which is deciphered by using the concept of probability.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"7372142965\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>18. For example recently my father decided to buy a car for the family.<br/>19. We had shortlisted two models from two different manufacturers but could not decide any further.<br/>20. That is when I used my probability skills to make the final decision.<br/>21. I gathered some data points about both the models such as service centres of each company, number of cars sold each year, number of accidents these two models were involved in.<br/>22. Then I used these data points to figure out that which car is more likely to last long with low maintenance cost using the probability method I learnt in school.</p>",
