  "prompts": [],
  "supporting_text": "<div class=\"entry-content\"><p><a href=\"../ielts-speaking-latest-makkar-cue-cards/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Latest Makkar cue cards with new solutions</strong></a></p><p>1. I am reticent person and like to keep things to myself.<br/>2. My parents are sometimes concerned about my introvert nature and always compare me to my younger brother who is antithesis of mine.<br/>3. He is absolutely gregarious and loves to socialize and can talk to even strangers for hours.<br/>4. He always knows how to break the ice and set the ball rolling.<br/>5. He has always been like this.<br/>6. When he was an infant he would blabber alone and my parents would enjoy his gibberish.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>7. I guess one of the reasons he can talk a lot is his inquisitive nature.<br/>8. He always has questions about everything and likes to get to the bottom it.<br/>9. He is not the one to take things on their face value and does not easily accept it if it does not make sense to him.<br/>10. He often argues with our parents on several topics and I have to say sometimes his arguments are hard to beat.<br/>11. Sure he argues but he ensures that he does not cross the line by disrespecting our parents.<br/>12. I particularly enjoy the discussion between him and one of my uncles who is a deeply religious person.<br/>13. Whenever he comes to our place it is inevitable that a conversation would start between these two around some religious topic and it would last for couple of hours.<br/>14. These conversations are entertaining as well as enlightening.<br/>15. My uncle is never affronted by his inquiries on the contrary he is impressed by his ability to question and learn.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>16. Since he asks a lot questions he has developed a perspective about almost everything.<br/>17. He is a sports fanatic and it is almost impossible to win an argument on sports against him.<br/>18. Once I accidentally mentioned that our cricket team captain should be dropped from the team because of his recent failures.<br/>19. The word dropped was enough to get him started after which he gave me a 15 minutes long lecture countering my opinion and at the end of which he managed to convince me otherwise.</p><p><a href=\"../ielts-speaking-latest-makkar-cue-cards/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Latest Makkar cue cards with new solutions</strong></a></p></div><p><a href=\"../ielts-speaking-latest-makkar-cue-cards/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Latest Makkar cue cards with new solutions</strong></a></p><p>1. I am reticent person and like to keep things to myself.<br/>2. My parents are sometimes concerned about my introvert nature and always compare me to my younger brother who is antithesis of mine.<br/>3. He is absolutely gregarious and loves to socialize and can talk to even strangers for hours.<br/>4. He always knows how to break the ice and set the ball rolling.<br/>5. He has always been like this.<br/>6. When he was an infant he would blabber alone and my parents would enjoy his gibberish.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>7. I guess one of the reasons he can talk a lot is his inquisitive nature.<br/>8. He always has questions about everything and likes to get to the bottom it.<br/>9. He is not the one to take things on their face value and does not easily accept it if it does not make sense to him.<br/>10. He often argues with our parents on several topics and I have to say sometimes his arguments are hard to beat.<br/>11. Sure he argues but he ensures that he does not cross the line by disrespecting our parents.<br/>12. I particularly enjoy the discussion between him and one of my uncles who is a deeply religious person.<br/>13. Whenever he comes to our place it is inevitable that a conversation would start between these two around some religious topic and it would last for couple of hours.<br/>14. These conversations are entertaining as well as enlightening.<br/>15. My uncle is never affronted by his inquiries on the contrary he is impressed by his ability to question and learn.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>16. Since he asks a lot questions he has developed a perspective about almost everything.<br/>17. He is a sports fanatic and it is almost impossible to win an argument on sports against him.<br/>18. Once I accidentally mentioned that our cricket team captain should be dropped from the team because of his recent failures.<br/>19. The word dropped was enough to get him started after which he gave me a 15 minutes long lecture countering my opinion and at the end of which he managed to convince me otherwise.</p><p><a href=\"../ielts-speaking-latest-makkar-cue-cards/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Latest Makkar cue cards with new solutions</strong></a></p>",
