  "supporting_text": "<div class=\"entry-content\"><p>1. For any individual life is a journey which is full of surprises.<br/>2. Every individual\u2019s life has some moments which he or she cherishes forever and some moments which are not so memorable.<br/>3. My life has been no different but fortunately I have had more great moments than not so great moments.<br/>4. Although it is difficult to pick one particular happy moment from my life because there have been so many, there is one particular experience which I will savor forever.<br/>5. It was the year when I completed my higher secondary school.<br/>6. In our education system higher secondary school is really crucial as its outcome decides the future course for any youngster.<br/>7. It lays the foundation of a bright career.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>8. Keeping this thing in mind I was determined to do well in that year, hence I started my preparation with utmost sincerity.<br/>9. For the first half of the year everything was on track, as I did well in all the house tests and had covered bulk of the course, earmarking second half for revision.<br/>10. However, it was around December when things started to go awry for me.<br/>11. During a club cricket match I slipped and fractured my left ankle.<br/>12. I was bedridden for a complete month because of which I could not attend my coaching classes where the revision batch had already started.<br/>13. I started panicking because my final exams were only two months away.<br/>14. And that is when my biggest pillar of strength, my family, helped me to go through that tough phase.<br/>15. My parents settled my nerves and instilled the confidence in me that despite these setback I will live up to their expectations.<br/>16. The fact that my family was beside me whatever the outcome really helped me to regain my focus.<br/>17. Although I missed my coaching classes, but to make up for that I doubled my effort at home.<br/>18. I kept abreast of everything happening in those classes through my friends.<br/>19. After a month my plaster was removed and I regained my mobility but was still not able to travel on my own because of which I had to continue my self-study at home.<br/>20. And then I finally appeared in my board exams.<br/>21. Exams came and went, and time just flew by.<br/>22. And then came the day of reckoning.<br/>23. My result was out and I would confess that I was not so confident about my performance, but when I saw my result on school\u2019s website was on cloud nine.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>24. I had managed to score 95% the second highest in my batch.<br/>25. My hard word had paid off and I will never forget that feeling of pride on the faces of my parents which easily makes it the best news I have heard in my life so far.</p><p>\u00a0</p><p><a href=\"../ielts-speaking-latest-makkar-cue-cards/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Latest Makkar Speaking CUE CARDS with NEW SOLUTIONS</strong></a></p></div><p>1. For any individual life is a journey which is full of surprises.<br/>2. Every individual\u2019s life has some moments which he or she cherishes forever and some moments which are not so memorable.<br/>3. My life has been no different but fortunately I have had more great moments than not so great moments.<br/>4. Although it is difficult to pick one particular happy moment from my life because there have been so many, there is one particular experience which I will savor forever.<br/>5. It was the year when I completed my higher secondary school.<br/>6. In our education system higher secondary school is really crucial as its outcome decides the future course for any youngster.<br/>7. It lays the foundation of a bright career.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>8. Keeping this thing in mind I was determined to do well in that year, hence I started my preparation with utmost sincerity.<br/>9. For the first half of the year everything was on track, as I did well in all the house tests and had covered bulk of the course, earmarking second half for revision.<br/>10. However, it was around December when things started to go awry for me.<br/>11. During a club cricket match I slipped and fractured my left ankle.<br/>12. I was bedridden for a complete month because of which I could not attend my coaching classes where the revision batch had already started.<br/>13. I started panicking because my final exams were only two months away.<br/>14. And that is when my biggest pillar of strength, my family, helped me to go through that tough phase.<br/>15. My parents settled my nerves and instilled the confidence in me that despite these setback I will live up to their expectations.<br/>16. The fact that my family was beside me whatever the outcome really helped me to regain my focus.<br/>17. Although I missed my coaching classes, but to make up for that I doubled my effort at home.<br/>18. I kept abreast of everything happening in those classes through my friends.<br/>19. After a month my plaster was removed and I regained my mobility but was still not able to travel on my own because of which I had to continue my self-study at home.<br/>20. And then I finally appeared in my board exams.<br/>21. Exams came and went, and time just flew by.<br/>22. And then came the day of reckoning.<br/>23. My result was out and I would confess that I was not so confident about my performance, but when I saw my result on school\u2019s website was on cloud nine.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>24. I had managed to score 95% the second highest in my batch.<br/>25. My hard word had paid off and I will never forget that feeling of pride on the faces of my parents which easily makes it the best news I have heard in my life so far.</p><p>\u00a0</p><p><a href=\"../ielts-speaking-latest-makkar-cue-cards/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Latest Makkar Speaking CUE CARDS with NEW SOLUTIONS</strong></a></p>",
