  "supporting_text": "<div class=\"entry-content\"><p><a href=\"../ielts-speaking-latest-makkar-cue-cards/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Latest Makkar cue cards with new solutions</strong></a></p><p>1. India is a land of rivers and lakes.<br/>2. Every state in my country has its own networks of rivers and lakes.<br/>3. All these rivers hold great significance in their respective states.<br/>4. Some are important because these are associated with the mythology and some are important from economic point of view.<br/>5. There is one river which holds a special place in the heart of every Indian and that is river Ganga.<br/>6. It is the longest river in my country with a span of 2000 km.<br/>7. It originates in the mountains of Himalaya and terminates by joining Indian Ocean in the bay of Bengal.<br/>8. In Hindu mythology Ganga is not considered just a river, it is revered as a goddess.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>9. There are many popular stories in which Ganga has been portrayed as a goddess and has been helping mankind since time immemorial.<br/>10. It is a tradition among Hindus to submerge the remains of a dead person after cremation in Ganga because it is believed that by doing this the departed soul is accepted by god and hence rests in peace forever.<br/>11. Ganga passes through more than 10 states in India.<br/>12. In each state it is called by a different name and every state has its own story linked with Ganga.<br/>13. But there is one common thing among all these states.<br/>14. In every state there is one or two religious places of great significance located on the banks of Ganga.<br/>15. While these shrines are primarily known for their religious importance, these have also become a great source of livelihood for the local citizens.<br/>16. Because of their religious value these temples are visited by millions of pilgrims every year from all over India.<br/>17. Such heavy footfall has turned these places into great tourist spots.<br/>18. Tourism has generated employment for local citizens and has helped them to raise their standard of living.<br/>19. Ganga has touched the lives of millions of people in my country and has contributed in some way or other positively.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>20. I just have one concern and that is the growing contamination of Ganga because of some human activities.<br/>21. Our government has taken note of it and has taken appropriate measures to keep our holy river clean.</p><p><a href=\"../ielts-speaking-latest-makkar-cue-cards/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Latest Makkar cue cards with new solutions</strong></a></p></div><p><a href=\"../ielts-speaking-latest-makkar-cue-cards/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Latest Makkar cue cards with new solutions</strong></a></p><p>1. India is a land of rivers and lakes.<br/>2. Every state in my country has its own networks of rivers and lakes.<br/>3. All these rivers hold great significance in their respective states.<br/>4. Some are important because these are associated with the mythology and some are important from economic point of view.<br/>5. There is one river which holds a special place in the heart of every Indian and that is river Ganga.<br/>6. It is the longest river in my country with a span of 2000 km.<br/>7. It originates in the mountains of Himalaya and terminates by joining Indian Ocean in the bay of Bengal.<br/>8. In Hindu mythology Ganga is not considered just a river, it is revered as a goddess.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>9. There are many popular stories in which Ganga has been portrayed as a goddess and has been helping mankind since time immemorial.<br/>10. It is a tradition among Hindus to submerge the remains of a dead person after cremation in Ganga because it is believed that by doing this the departed soul is accepted by god and hence rests in peace forever.<br/>11. Ganga passes through more than 10 states in India.<br/>12. In each state it is called by a different name and every state has its own story linked with Ganga.<br/>13. But there is one common thing among all these states.<br/>14. In every state there is one or two religious places of great significance located on the banks of Ganga.<br/>15. While these shrines are primarily known for their religious importance, these have also become a great source of livelihood for the local citizens.<br/>16. Because of their religious value these temples are visited by millions of pilgrims every year from all over India.<br/>17. Such heavy footfall has turned these places into great tourist spots.<br/>18. Tourism has generated employment for local citizens and has helped them to raise their standard of living.<br/>19. Ganga has touched the lives of millions of people in my country and has contributed in some way or other positively.</p><p><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins></p><p>20. I just have one concern and that is the growing contamination of Ganga because of some human activities.<br/>21. Our government has taken note of it and has taken appropriate measures to keep our holy river clean.</p><p><a href=\"../ielts-speaking-latest-makkar-cue-cards/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Latest Makkar cue cards with new solutions</strong></a></p>",
